title: Coalition Affairs
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; coalition_affairs_timer = 5
view-if: psoe_in_government = 1 and coalition_dissent >= 1 and coalition_affairs_timer = 0 and (in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front)
card-image: img/muller_cabinet.jpg
#subtitle: There is dissent within our coalition.

= Coalition Affairs

Our coalition is in trouble. [? if in_republican_socialist : Our republican partners in Izquierda Republicana are growing uneasy at the pace of our reforms, and are muttering about withdrawing their support. ?][? if in_popular_front : The tensions between our own Caballerista and Prietista wings over how closely to bind ourselves to a government we do not fully control are boiling over, and Izquierda Republicana is wary of the PSOE's continued street mobilization. ?]

How do we reduce tensions within the coalition?

- @promise_cuts: Agree to slow the pace of reform to ease our partners' fears.
- @resources: Use our party resources to smooth things over.
- @no_change: Take none of these actions.
- @easy_discard


@promise_cuts
on-arrival: industrial_psoe -= 5; unemployed_psoe -= 6; industrial_pce += 5; unemployed_pce += 3; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 5; land_reform -= 1 if land_reform > 0; budget += 1; coalition_dissent = 0; izq_rep_relation += 8; radical_relation += 5

Fine. By slowing the pace of land reform, we have reduced dissent within the coalition - at the cost of our own base's patience.

@resources
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 2: We do not have enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 2; coalition_dissent -= 1

By quietly smoothing things over with our coalition partners, we can make our policies more palatable to them. Some would call this the ordinary business of coalition government; others might call it something less flattering.

@no_change

No. We will not do this.
